{"skill":{"slug":"docker-essentials","displayName":"Docker Essentials"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769692040015,"changelog":"docker-essentials 1.0.0\n\n- Initial release with a comprehensive guide to essential Docker commands and workflows.\n- Covers container lifecycle management, debugging, image operations, Compose, networking, volumes, and system cleanup.\n- Includes common workflow examples, multi-stage build patterns, and handy flag references.\n- Links to official Docker, Dockerfile, and Compose references for further documentation.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6281,"sha256":"bf8120febd5275b0b1d5f996a4cbed4f52b7d99895271604f87f02b58e7d96a9","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2328,"sha256":"6bc2ccf4d13bd5849b47b7aaf088dd4986a298ddc0cbbdd127043ad35a7a244c","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789023465212,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"4345a9f7557790ab2c9e7ba6248234163a81f514e098f284e22d68c53d4fb6ff","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/4345a9f7557790ab2c9e7ba6248234163a81f514e098f284e22d68c53d4fb6ff","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: docker-essentials\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides a comprehensive guide to essential Docker commands and workflows, as described in `SKILL.md`. All commands and instructions are standard Docker operations, clearly aligned with the stated purpose of container management and debugging. There is no evidence of prompt injection attempts against the agent, data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence, or obfuscation. The `_meta.json` file contains standard metadata, and the `SKILL.md` frontmatter correctly declares the dependency on the `docker` binary, which is expected for this type of skill.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160293755},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":55,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":18,"checkedAt":1789023465212},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a straightforward Docker command reference, but users should be careful with cleanup commands, registry pushes, exposed ports, and example credentials.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Docker access can materially affect local containers, images, volumes, networks, and published services, which is proportionate for this Docker-focused skill but requires careful user judgment.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The inspected package is a Markdown skill with frontmatter metadata requiring the docker binary; no install script, embedded executable, remote payload fetch, or tool override was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions include destructive Docker commands such as container, image, volume, Compose, and system cleanup; they are labeled as remove or clean up operations, but the skill gives limited warning about irreversible data loss.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill itself does not establish persistence or elevated privileges, but examples can create long-running containers, persistent volumes, and host port bindings when a user chooses to run them.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact's purpose is Docker command guidance, and its capabilities are limited to documented, user-directed Docker examples for containers, images, Compose, networks, volumes, debugging, and common workflows.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want a Docker command cheat sheet. Before running examples, review cleanup commands because volumes and images may contain important data, avoid pushing images that might include secrets or private code, pin production images, and replace the sample database password and port binding with secure local settings.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The flagged prune, remove, and down -v commands are standard Docker administration operations and are visibly described as removal or cleanup commands; the accepted concern is missing stronger caution language, not hidden or automatic destruction.\n[RP1] expected: The Docker image references are common command examples, including some unpinned images; this is normal for a quick reference, though production use should pin trusted tags or digests.\n[T09] expected: The PostgreSQL example is a plausible Docker workflow, but the placeholder password and broad port publication could be unsafe if copied into a real or exposed environment without changes.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789023465212}}}}}